mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><em>Pharmacology</em> is a professional course for undergraduate students majoring in pharmacy. The course primarily covers fundamental knowledge such as the pharmacological mechanisms, pharmacokinetic characteristics, clinical applications, adverse effects, and drug interactions of major drug categories, with a focus on the pharmacological features of representative drugs in each category.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
